# Keep the build context small and reproducible
node_modules
dist
.git
.github
# Maven output only — NOT a bare "target" (the source package
# com.spiramindscape.backend.target must stay in the build context).
backend/target
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
tests-e2e
# Root-level book folder. In .dockerignore an unanchored "grow" only matches
# the root anyway, but keep it explicit so it's never copied into a pattern
# with gitignore semantics (see .gcloudignore, where that broke the deploy).
/grow
docs
specs
**/*.md
# …EXCEPT the prompts, which are runtime resources that merely happen to be Markdown.
#
# `PromptResources` loads `prompts/grow/coach-method.md` from the classpath at construction and
# **fails startup** when it is missing — deliberately, because a coach silently running without
# its method is worse than a boot failure. With the blanket `**/*.md` above and nothing to undo
# it, `COPY backend/src src` put an EMPTY `prompts/grow/` into the image, the jar shipped without
# the file, and Cloud Run rejected every revision with "container failed to start and listen on
# the port" — three deploys in a row, with nothing in the build log pointing at a Markdown rule
# (2026-08-27).
#
# Order matters: in .dockerignore the LAST matching pattern wins, so this negation has to stay
# below the exclusion.
!backend/src/main/resources/prompts/**
